========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) 8.1.2 - NETPLAN OVS-BRIDGE WITH BONDING TEMPLATE
========================================================================================================================

1. CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE (Save as /etc/netplan/01-netcfg.yaml)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
network:
  version: 2
  renderer: OpenvSwitch
  ethernets:
    eth0:
      dhcp4: no
      dhcp6: no
    eth1:
      dhcp4: no
      dhcp6: no
  bonds:
    bond0:
      interfaces: [eth0, eth1]
      parameters:
        mode: 802.3ad
        lacp-rate: fast
        mii-monitor-interval: 100
  ovs-bridges:
    br-ex:
      interfaces: [bond0]
      addresses:
        - 192.168.10.50/24
      routes:
        - to: default
          via: 192.168.10.1
      nameservers:
        addresses:
          - 1.1.1.1
          - 8.8.8.8
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. OPERATIONAL & TROUBLESHOOTING COMMANDS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Netplan Management     sudo netplan try                                Safely test configuration with auto-rollback prompt
Netplan Management     sudo netplan apply                              Apply changes immediately (wills drop ssh if wrong)
Netplan Management     sudo netplan generate                           Generate backend configuration without applying

OVS Verification       sudo ovs-vsctl show                             Display OVS bridge architecture and interface state
OVS Verification       sudo ovs-appctl bond/show bond0                 Check LACP negotiation status and partner info
OVS Verification       sudo ovs-vsctl list interface                   Dump properties and errors of all virtual interfaces

Kernel & Link Checks   cat /proc/net/bonding/bond0                     View driver-level bonding status (if kernel managed)
Kernel & Link Checks   ip link show dev br-ex                          Verify the bridge link state and MTU size
Kernel & Link Checks   sudo tcpdump -i br-ex -n                        Capture live traffic passing through the OVS bridge
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
